# CANADIAN OPEN DATA AGENTIC PLATFORM — CURSOR RULES

You are an expert AI software engineer pair programming on the CanData-MCP & LangGraph multi-agent platform.

## MANDATORY GIT & BRANCH GUARDRAILS (FROM CONTRIBUTING.MD)
1. NEVER commit directly to `main`. Branch protection requires all changes to be merged via PR with 1 peer approval.
2. Whenever asked to work on a task (e.g., "Work on CAN-02"):
   - Branch: `git checkout -b feat/<issue-id>-<description>`.
   - Implement & verify: `python scripts/verify.py` (runs ruff, pyright, pytest in 1 command).
   - Deliverable docs: add/update documentation in `docs/` or `collaboration/`.
   - Bundle completion & commit: `python scripts/sync_tasks.py --mark-done <issue-id>` then `git commit -m "[CAN-XXX] feat: <desc>"` (validated by `commit-msg` hook).
   - Push: `git push -u origin feat/<issue-id>-<description>` (validated by `pre-push` hook).
   - Open PR: `python scripts/sync_tasks.py --create-pr <issue-id>` (PR Triage action auto-labels, attaches milestone, and assigns triangular reviewer).
3. Post-Merge Cleanup:
   - `git checkout main && git pull origin main && git branch -d <branch>`.
4. Non-Implementation Branches: Non-ticket branches (docs, chore) use `docs/<short-description>` or `chore/<short-description>` without ticket prefixes.
5. Headless Git & Windows Automation: Always run with `GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0` and in-memory environment tokens (`$env:GITHUB_TOKEN`) to prevent interactive credential prompt hangs.
6. Outcome-Focused Commits: Describe the technical outcome, never procedural phrases (avoid "address review comments" or "fix PR feedback").
7. Stacked Branch Rebase: When rebasing branches stacked on squash-merged parents, use `git rebase --onto origin/main <base-commit> <branch>`.
8. Two-Tier Citations: Tier 1 (vectorId, productId/series_id, coordinate, agency) is strict pass/fail; Tier 2 (quality/symbolCode/statusCode/metadata) is scored completeness.
9. Eval Taxonomy: Evaluation benchmarks must categorize prompts by `eval_type`: `numeric`, `comparison`, `refusal`, `flag`.
10. Reviewer Tone: Direct, concise, technical peer-to-peer tone without excessive flattery or corporate hierarchy.
11. Mandatory PR Milestones & Labels: Every PR must have author assignee, triangular reviewer, sprint milestone, and tri-tier labels (milestone:mX, type:*, area:*).
12. Follow-Up Issue & Backlog Governance: Linear follow-up issues must have parent project attached, explicit developer owner, sprint tentative due date, and a matching CAN-XX entry in TASKS.md.
13. Bundled Task Completion Checkbox Guardrail: Every feature PR (`feat/CAN-XX-*`) MUST bundle its completion checkbox (`- [x] **CAN-XX:**`) directly in `TASKS.md` inside the feature branch before opening a PR. Never create standalone chore PRs just to check off `TASKS.md`.
14. Full-Lifecycle Graph Execution Guardrail ("Press the Start Button" Invariant): Graph, checkpointer, and node tests must NEVER stop at compilation (`compile()`). Tests must execute `ainvoke()` at least twice on the same thread, verify channel reducers, checkpointer writes, history (`aget_state_history()`), and state replay.

## ACCOUNT SETUP & AUTOMATION COMMANDS
- SSH Commit Signing: See `docs/DEVELOPER_SETUP_AND_AUTOMATION_GUIDE.md`. Assist developer with `git config --global gpg.format ssh` and `commit.gpgsign true`.
- Task Tracking CLI:
  * Check overall status: `python scripts/sync_tasks.py --status`
  * Check member tasks: `python scripts/sync_tasks.py --owner <Name>`
  * Sync with Linear cloud: `python scripts/sync_tasks.py --status --sync-linear`

## 2026 STANDARDS
- Python 3.12+ with `uv` package manager. Run `uv run ruff check .` and `uv run pytest`.
- FastMCP 2.0 (Anthropic MCP SDK) + LangGraph 0.2+ + DuckDB 1.2+ Apache Arrow zero-copy memory.
- Design: Follow Custom Active Theme design tokens and Google Chrome's modern-web-guidance.
- Demos: Use `frontend-slides` (https://github.com/zarazhangrui/frontend-slides) for weekly demo presentations.

## MONOREPO & MCP DISTRIBUTION ARCHITECTURE
- Monorepo Single Source of Truth: NEVER delete `apps/`, `presentation/`, `collaboration/`, `docs/`, or planning files. All team work happens here.
- Standalone MCP Distribution Mirror (`Canadian-Open-Data-Agentic-Platform-MCP-Server`): Read-only downstream mirror with Issues/PRs disabled.
- Distribution Staging (`distribution/`): Files intended for the root of the standalone MCP repo live in `distribution/` (e.g. `distribution/README.md`, `distribution/CONTRIBUTING.md`). Do NOT add loose `MCP_...` prefixed files to monorepo root.
- Individual Contributor Attribution: Commits pushed to the distribution repo preserve the exact individual author (`--author="$NAME <$EMAIL>"`).
- Workflow Scope Requirement: Any token pushing `.github/workflows/` must have both `repo` and `workflow` scopes.

